{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Elohim called the light Day.</b> Even though there was not yet a time of light and <b>darkness</b> governed in the manner that it is governed among us — the time that we now call by the name day and by the name <b>night</b>." "<b>And there was evening and there was morning.</b> Even though He separated the light and the darkness to serve at alternating intervals without the revolution of a sphere, He separated them gradually, so that there was between them a time of evening at the onset of night and a time of morning at the onset of day."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:11:16.593780241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}